\SourceFootnote{1 ter}{\LayerTarget{tohoku:section:1.3:footnote:1ter:text}%
A more natural definition of the image of $u$, to
tell the truth, would be to take the smallest subobject $B'$ of $B$ (if one
exists) such that $u$ comes from a morphism from $A$ to $B'$. This definition
is equivalent to the one given in the text only when $\mathbf{C}$ is an \textit{abelian}
category (cf. 1.4.)}

